      "text": "Best Practices for Provider Agnosticism",
      "fontSize": 43.07368421052632,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 22,
      "frameId": "Ns8tkcfQ1gouZGlgHC0ly",
      "roundness": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Best Practices for Provider Agnosticism",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.1666666666666667
    },
    {
      "id": "1rwgfQa-ZMH-yvkUVQ1EU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -10625.037222410805,
      "y": 11879.38041686343,
      "width": 2153.684210526316,
      "height": 179.47368421052633,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "strokeSharpness": "sharp",
      "seed": 1400266833,
      "version": 186,
      "versionNonce": 443740735,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783988529395,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Avoid Proprietary Orchestration: Do not use AWS Step Functions or Azure Logic Apps for core logic. Use Temporal or Apache Airflow.\n2. Standardize the Interface: Build adapter layers (e.g., an internal EventPublisher interface) instead of importing AWS SDKs directly into business logic.\n3. Keep Compute Stateless: Ensure workloads spin up instantly, handle events, and push state to a managed database or distributed cache like Redis.",
      "fontSize": 32.305263157894736,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 16,
      "frameId": "Ns8tkcfQ1gouZGlgHC0ly",
      "roundness": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Avoid Proprietary Orchestration: Do not use AWS Step Functions or Azure Logic Apps for core logic. Use Temporal or Apache Airflow.\n2. Standardize the Interface: Build adapter layers (e.g., an internal EventPublisher interface) instead of importing AWS SDKs directly into business logic.\n3. Keep Compute Stateless: Ensure workloads spin up instantly, handle events, and push state to a managed database or distributed cache like Redis.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.851851851851852
    },
    {
      "id": "VzLFxCTnbLvos-RLT_EN0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -10360.266317583808,
      "y": 7928.622103899454,
      "width": 1751.8426724137933,
      "height": 92.74461206896552,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
